What if `ttype&15 != 0` and `ttype&128` is set? Then `desc[tnum<<4].buf` is allocated. `i = (tnum<<4) | (ttype&15) != tnum<<4`. So `desc[i].buf` is a different slot. Fine.

What if `ttype&64` is set but `ttype&128` is NOT set? Then `tnum` is not incremented, and `desc[tnum<<4]` is not zeroed. `i = (tnum<<4) | (ttype&15)`. `desc[i].buf` is freed and re-allocated. Fine.

